## 🎯 Day 54 Objective

Day 53 produced a threat model. A threat model that stops at a control matrix is a document. This is the other half: **where each control actually gets enforced, on which hook, with what verdict.**

OWASP's [Agent Control Standard (ACS)](https://genai.owasp.org/resource/agent-control-standard-acs/) — moved under the GenAI Security Project in September 2026 — is the missing implementation layer. Every governance framework agrees on *what* is required (runtime visibility, intervention capability, auditable controls). None of them specifies *how*. ACS does.

Deliverable: ACS primer → hook inventory → ASI01–ASI10 enforcement mapping → declarative policy pack → telemetry spec → AgBOM baseline → honest coverage-gap analysis → phased adoption roadmap.

