## 🧩 1. ACS in 90 Seconds

ACS rests on a claim worth stating plainly: **agents must be inspectable, traceable, and instrumentable.** Three pillars, three specs.

| Pillar | Spec | What it delivers | Built on |
|--------|------|------------------|----------|
| **Inspect** | AgBOM | Dynamic Agent Bill of Materials — every tool, model, capability, knowledge source, dependency. Updates in real time as agents discover new tools or modify capabilities | CycloneDX, SPDX, SWID |
| **Trace** | Observability | Structured trace of every action, decision, reasoning step. Agent-specific semantic conventions; security events mapped for SIEM | OpenTelemetry, OCSF |
| **Instrument** | Runtime hooks | Standardized middleware hooks at every agent decision point. A Guardian Agent intercepts, evaluates against policy, returns **allow / deny / modify** — inline, before the action reaches production | ACS schema |

### The three-tier control model

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ TIER 1 — PLATFORM LAYER                                         │
│ Agent framework exposes standardized hooks. One-time work.      │
│ The platform does NOT implement policy. It exposes hooks.       │
│ ── That is the entire ask. ──                                   │
└────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                             │  hook fires with action context
┌────────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐
│ TIER 2 — OPEN-SOURCE ENFORCEMENT LAYER (Guardian Agent)         │
│ Framework-agnostic SDK reads declarative policy and evaluates:  │
│   input validation • tool-call authorization                    │
│   output filtering • adversarial detection                      │
│ Switching frameworks does not mean rewriting safety logic.      │
└────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                             │  pluggable classifiers
┌────────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐
│ TIER 3 — ENTERPRISE CUSTOMIZATION LAYER                         │
│ Your own detectors: PHI, PCI, data-sensitivity models,          │
│ existing DLP/SIEM tooling. No platform change required.         │
└────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                             │
                    ┌────────▼────────┐
                    │ ALLOW  DENY     │
                    │      MODIFY     │
                    └─────────────────┘
```

**Why this architecture matters for governance:** the enforcement point is *outside* the agent. System prompts are not controls — they are requests. Model improvements do not cover adversarial edge cases. Proprietary guardrails create lock-in. ACS makes the control plane declarative, portable, and auditable as an artifact separate from the agent it governs.

