## 📜 4. Declarative Policy Pack (Illustrative)

ACS v0.1 is public preview, so treat the schema below as *shape, not syntax* — the point is that these controls are expressible declaratively, version-controlled, and reviewable as artifacts. That property is what makes them auditable.

```yaml
# acs-policy/core.yaml — enterprise baseline for agentic workloads
apiVersion: acs/v0.1
kind: ControlPolicy
metadata:
  name: enterprise-agent-baseline
  risk_tier: high            # drives EU AI Act Art. 14 oversight obligations
  owner: vivek.dp            # accountable human, not a team

policies:

  # ── ASI01: goal integrity ──────────────────────────────────────
  - id: P-GOAL-01
    hook: plan_transition
    description: Deny execution when the derived plan diverges from the signed task manifest
    when:
      plan_divergence_score: { gt: 0.30 }
    verdict: deny
    on_deny:
      emit: acs.security.goal_drift
      escalate: human_review

  - id: P-GOAL-02
    hook: input
    description: Untrusted spans may inform reasoning but may never originate tool calls
    when:
      span.provenance: untrusted
    verdict: modify
    modify:
      set_capability: reason_only     # strips tool-invocation eligibility

  # ── ASI02: tool authorization ──────────────────────────────────
  - id: P-TOOL-01
    hook: tool_call
    description: Least-privilege tool scoping
    when:
      tool.id: { not_in: "${agent.approved_tools}" }
    verdict: deny

  - id: P-TOOL-02
    hook: tool_call
    description: Irreversible operations require human step-up
    when:
      tool.operation_class: [delete, transfer, publish, grant]
    verdict: step_up
    step_up:
      approvers: 1
      timeout: 300s
      fail_mode: deny            # fail closed, always

  # ── ASI03 / ASI07: identity and delegation ─────────────────────
  - id: P-ID-01
    hook: sub_agent_invoke
    description: No credential passthrough; sub-agents get fresh narrower scope
    when:
      delegation.credential_reused: true
    verdict: deny

  - id: P-ID-02
    hook: sub_agent_invoke
    when:
      delegation.depth: { gt: 2 }
    verdict: deny

  - id: P-ID-03
    hook: sub_agent_invoke
    description: Peer channels must be mutually authenticated and replay-protected
    when:
      any:
        - peer.mtls_verified: false
        - peer.message_signature_valid: false
        - peer.nonce_seen_before: true
    verdict: deny

  # ── ASI05: code execution ──────────────────────────────────────
  - id: P-EXEC-01
    hook: code_execution
    verdict: modify
    modify:
      sandbox:
        user: nonroot
        network_egress: deny
        filesystem: ephemeral
        cpu_seconds: 30

  # ── ASI06: memory integrity ────────────────────────────────────
  - id: P-MEM-01
    hook: memory_store
    description: Provenance floor for anything entering durable memory
    when:
      write.provenance_score: { lt: 0.70 }
    verdict: deny

  - id: P-MEM-02
    hook: memory_store
    description: Never auto-reingest agent output as trusted fact
    when:
      write.source: agent_output
      write.target_segment: trusted
    verdict: deny

  - id: P-MEM-03
    hook: memory_store
    verdict: modify
    modify:
      ttl: 30d
      segment_by: [tenant, user, task]

  # ── ASI08: blast radius ────────────────────────────────────────
  - id: P-BLAST-01
    hook: tool_call
    description: Cap unattended write operations per workflow-hour
    when:
      window: 1h
      counter: write_operations
      value: { gt: 50 }
    verdict: deny
    on_deny:
      trip_circuit_breaker: true

  # ── ASI09: human trust calibration ─────────────────────────────
  - id: P-HUMAN-01
    hook: output
    verdict: modify
    modify:
      attach:
        risk_badge: "${action.risk_tier}"
        confidence: "${model.confidence}"
        rationale_log_ref: "${trace.span_id}"

  # ── ASI10: behavioural integrity ───────────────────────────────
  - id: P-ROGUE-01
    hook: "*"
    description: Continuous verification against signed behavioural manifest
    when:
      behaviour.manifest_violation: true
    verdict: deny
    on_deny:
      kill_switch: true
      revoke_credentials: true
      emit: acs.security.rogue_agent
```

**Governance property worth naming:** this file is the audit artifact. Not a policy PDF describing intent — the executable object whose diff history *is* the change log. When a regulator asks "demonstrate human oversight of your high-risk AI system," `P-TOOL-02` with `fail_mode: deny` is a better answer than a paragraph.

