## 📦 6. AgBOM Baseline

Static SBOMs assume the software doesn't change itself. Agents discover new tools, connect to new MCP servers, and modify their own capabilities at runtime — so the inventory has to be dynamic.

Minimum viable AgBOM for a governance gate:

- **Models** — provider, exact version, pinned or floating, hosting region
- **Prompts** — system prompt hash and version lineage
- **Tools** — every tool and MCP server, signature status, scope granted
- **Knowledge sources** — RAG indices, datasets, classification, refresh cadence
- **Memory stores** — type, segmentation scheme, retention/TTL
- **Sub-agents** — peer agents callable, delegation scope, max depth
- **Runtime** — sandbox profile, egress policy, execution limits
- **Human owner** — a named accountable individual

Every entry needs a **change event**, not just a snapshot. "Agent connected to an MCP server not present at approval time" is a governance trigger, and only a dynamic AgBOM can raise it.

