## 🗺️ 8. Phased Adoption Roadmap

| Phase | Scope | Exit criterion |
|-------|-------|----------------|
| **0 — Inventory** (wks 1–2) | Build AgBOM for every agent already in production. Expect to find agents nobody approved | Complete inventory with named owners |
| **1 — Trace only** (wks 3–6) | Instrument hooks in observe mode. Emit telemetry. Enforce nothing | Baseline behavioural profile per agent; drift threshold calibrated on real data |
| **2 — Enforce two hooks** (wks 7–12) | Turn on `deny` at **tool call** and **memory store** — six of ten ASI risks, per §3 | Zero false-deny incidents over 2 weeks; policy pack in version control |
| **3 — Gate the plan transition** (Q2) | Goal-drift enforcement. Highest value, hardest tuning | Drift detection validated by red team, not by absence of alerts |
| **4 — Full surface + containment** (Q3) | All hooks; kill switch tested end-to-end including credential revocation propagation | Tabletop exercise passed; blast-radius caps live |
| **5 — Procurement leverage** (ongoing) | ACS hook exposure becomes a vendor requirement | Contract language; no un-instrumented agent platforms approved |

Phase 1 is non-negotiable and the most commonly skipped. Enforcing policy on an uncalibrated threshold generates false denials, which destroys organizational trust in the control plane — and a control plane the business has learned to route around is worse than none.

